// #4429: `bit_rt_safepoint` preserves the WHOLE allocatable integer file
// (x1..x8, x12..x15, x19..x28 on arm64), not just the calling convention's
// callee-saved subset, and republishes it in the snapshot the collector scans.
//
// WHY THIS LIVES IN _tests_/stress AND NOT _tests_/cases. The property only
// exists at a back-edge poll that actually FIRES, and a poll fires on the cold
// arm — when the attention word is set. `BIT_GC=stress` makes `gcShouldCollect`
// unconditionally true, so every back edge in `pressure` below takes the `bl`.
// Under the default policy this program allocates almost nothing and would
// collect zero times, which is why it cannot be a golden case: it would pass
// without ever executing the thing it is written to check.
//
// AND WHY THE LOOP CONTAINS NO CALL AND NO ALLOCATION. That is the whole
// construction, not a simplification. A call inside the loop is a full clobber
// point (compiler/regalloc.bit's `AllocPoints.clobbers`), which puts every
// loop-carried value back into x19..x28 and makes the program silent about
// #4429. With only the poll crossing the back edge, the allocator draws from
// the widened file and the values below land in x0..x15.
//
// WHAT IT KILLS. Revert the arm64 payload in `runtime/stw/stwpoll.bit` to the
// pre-#4429 fourteen words (x19..x28 only) while leaving the compiler's
// `isPollSavedInt` widened — i.e. land one half of #4429 and not the other —
// and every value the allocator placed in x1..x8/x12..x15 is destroyed by the
// first poll that fires. The sum below then comes out wrong, at exit 0.
//
// WHAT IT DOES NOT KILL, said here rather than left to be discovered. It does
// not prove the ROOTING half — that a GC reference the poll's stack map names
// in a widened register is really found by `gcScanSnapshot`. A missed root
// frees a buffer whose bytes then stay intact until something else allocates
// that slot, and this loop deliberately allocates nothing. The programs that do
// catch a missing register root are `schedgrowdarwin`/`schedgrowdemanddarwin`
// (see runtime/gc/stackmap.bit's #4111 note, which mutation-proved exactly
// that), and they run in this same batch against the same widened file.
//
// SIX buffers, read on every lap, is not arbitrary: each contributes a `buf`
// and a `len` that must survive the back edge, so twelve values plus `acc`,
// `k` and `laps` is comfortably past the ten registers x19..x28 offers. Five
// buffers would fit and prove nothing.

fn pressure(laps: int): int {
  let a = []i64(16)
  let b = []i64(16)
  let c = []i64(16)
  let d = []i64(16)
  let e = []i64(16)
  let g = []i64(16)
  let i = 0
  while (i < 16) {
    a[i] = i + 1
    b[i] = i + 17
    c[i] = i + 33
    d[i] = i + 49
    e[i] = i + 65
    g[i] = i + 81
    i = i + 1
  }

  // The hot loop: no call, no allocation, six live slices. `& 15` rather than
  // `% 16` so no division guard is emitted and the body stays call-free.
  let acc = 0
  let k = 0
  while (k < laps) {
    let j = k & 15
    acc = acc + a[j] + b[j] + c[j] + d[j] + e[j] + g[j]
    k = k + 1
  }
  return acc
}

// One full cycle of j = 0..15 sums to 6*(0+..+15) + (1+17+33+49+65+81)*16
// = 720 + 3936 = 4656. 2048 laps is 128 whole cycles: 128 * 4656 = 595968.
fn main() {
  print("${pressure(2048)}\n")
}
